+  #
+  # WHY NOT `continue-on-error` ON THE STEP. It would fix the conclusion and
+  # nothing else: the roll's failure would render as a neutral, near-invisible
+  # annotation inside a green job, and it would still be unreachable by a
+  # re-run. A separate job keeps the failure LOUD and RED where it belongs
